  "headline": "Mondrian conformal novelty (Vovk-Lindsay-Nouretdinov-Gammerman 2003) over the 443-member SHA-locked OpenPoly corpus partitioned into 4 Bemis-Murcko ring-system classes (ACYCLIC 255 / ALIPHATIC_RING 42 / CARBOAROMATIC 117 / HETEROAROMATIC 29): the Morgan(r2,2048) anchor reproduces every signed candidate NN EXACTLY (max err 0.00e+00), then H0 ('marginal conformal is already scaffold-conditionally valid') is REFUTED -- 3 category x alpha cells breach nominal, worst HETEROAROMATIC@alpha=0.05 at 0.1724 (3.45x nominal, exact-binomial p=1.36e-02). Mondrian restores conditional validity in 4/4 categories at all 4 alphas and in all 3 representations. Candidate count at alpha=0.05: fixed-0.40 5/5, marginal 4/5, Mondrian 4/5; no candidate verdict flips.",
  "hypothesis_evaluation": {
    "interpretation": "Scaffold-conditional coverage is a strictly stronger and more honest guarantee for a novelty screen used to support IP claims: it is the per-chemistry error rate, not the portfolio average. Where the marginal detector over-flags a sparse scaffold class, every 'novel' verdict in that class carries a higher true false-novelty rate than its stated alpha -- the exact direction that manufactures unearned novelty. Mondrian conditioning removes that, at a quantified cost in resolution for small categories.",
    "prior_audit_claim": "conformal-anomaly-detection-v1: 4/5 conformal-novel at alpha=0.05 with MARGINAL validity.",
    "signed_claim": "5/5 canonical DGEBA epoxy-amine hardeners are NOVEL vs the OpenPoly corpus (NN Tanimoto < 0.40).",
    "verdict": "H0_REFUTED__MARGINAL_CONFORMAL_IS_NOT_SCAFFOLD_CONDITIONALLY_VALID__MONDRIAN_REPAIRS"
  },
