    "conditionally_valid_all_categories_all_alphas": true,
    "residual_breaches": [],
    "resolution_limit": "Mondrian p is bounded below by 1/(n_k+1), so a category cannot certify novelty at any alpha <= 1/(n_k+1) regardless of how alien the molecule is. This is the price of conditioning and it is reported per category rather than hidden."
  },
  "non_circularity": "The Morgan(r2,2048)/Tanimoto lane reproduces the independently-signed per-candidate NN Tanimoto to <1e-12 before any conformal or Mondrian layer is applied. The Mondrian taxonomy is a structure-only function (ring systems), computed without reading Tg, novelty labels, or the signed verdict, so it cannot import the answer. Corpus is the SHA-locked rights-clean OpenPoly CSV, read-only. The p-value adds no free parameter: it is a rank statistic inside the object's own category.",
